  "description": "Browser tests for a Rask app. RaskSite<Program> starts the app's own build as a process of its own on a free port, over a database of its own, waits for its health check, and hands out pages in one shared Chromium — signed out, or await site.SignedIn(site.Admin), signed in once and reused. await site.Walk(\"/orders\") opens a page and fails on a console or page error, a failed request, a not-found or forbidden answer, a dropped connection, or a page wider than a phone; RaskSite.Pages<Program>() lists every page the app's route table can open without a value, for a walk-every-page test. await page.WaitForRask() waits until a page has settled: every event answered and its render on the page, every navigation landed, the connection open, what was typed sent — no sleeps, no DOM-quiet windows. The Rask answer to Laravel Dusk.",
